# Commercial S9 credential-baseline preflight diagnosis

## Observed

The first server-side S9 preflight stopped before service mutation with
`CREDENTIAL_OWNER_DRIFT`.

## Root cause

The new S9 controller expected `root:chatops` / `0640`, while the verified and
currently healthy S8 baseline stores both the Telegram token and database DSN
as single-link regular files owned by `root:root` with mode `0600`.

The S8 and S9 services consume these files through systemd `LoadCredential`, so
the service account does not require direct filesystem access.

## Resolution

Bind the S9 preflight to the stricter existing `root:root` / `0600` baseline.
Do not mutate either credential file. Keep the link-count and regular-file
guards unchanged.

## Rollback

Revert this correction commit. No server service, database, credential, or
runtime state was changed by the failed preflight.
